def record(sid,details,remaining=(),extra_scopes=()):
 row=by[sid]
 event={'id':'full-receiving-proof-20261117','reader':META,'scope':'Entire displayed statement and proof, with the operative pre-statement definitions; nested inputs followed or separately identified.','details':details,'extra_source_scopes':list(extra_scopes),'outcome':'complete receiving proof independently followed; no mathematical defect found in its stated scope','remaining_dependencies':list(remaining)}
 row['new_check_events']=[e for e in row['new_check_events'] if e['id']!=event['id']]+[event]
 row['status']=event['outcome']
 row['remaining_dependencies']=list(remaining)

record('E.1.4','Read E1.1–3 definitions and the whole E1.4 proof. The elliptic projection is smooth over X minus W and has its actual section; section loops die in the embedded simply connected X. The two finite elliptic monodromies have primitive combined coinvariant relation matrix, so pi1 vanishes. Euler is the six toric zero-strata. Rechecked the Leray rows, the skyscraper kernel in q4, all pulled-back sphere transgressions and the independent permanent elliptic-orientation class. In particular r4 is fixed at2 by b3=b5 Poincare duality, not by assuming degeneration. The finite affine quotient H1 presentation has the correctly signed relation m*a-(v,0).', ['E1.3 external Chen/pure-weight source gate is owned by maps_audit; original X integral topology is in PaperI','fourfolds_checks.py and full exterior-page checker rerun records to integrate'], ['fourfolds.tex lines1–294: complete construction and cusp-specialization statement/proof read as operative context'])
record('E.2.1','Recomputed the root-stack degree formula for k=0,1,-1,-2 and the split direct images from the actual cusp cup product and invariant covector. K_X=L^-6 and Weierstrass adjunction plus the actual small crepant resolution give K_Z=Pi*L^-5. Fibres of Pi remain dimension one even over the toric deeper strata; flatness and relative duality give R1Pi*O=L^-1. The section splits the derived unit, so the two acyclic root twists yield h0q=(1,1,0,0,0). A meromorphic trivialization of L makes x generically degree two to X×P1, proving a=2 via symmetric functions. Read the original Jia–Meng Theorem1.1/Remark1.2 p2, Esole–Kang equations1.2–1.4 pp3–4, and Peters–Sterk Theorem2.2.1 with full proof p61. Checked c1=0, c4=6, c2²=2, signature2 and the positive rank-two unimodular lattice I2. Only universal characteristic polynomials are imported from the algebraic Weierstrass source.', ['E1.4 and E1.3 dependencies as separately scoped','Original root-stack analytic duality/base-change already opened in CDP records'], ['Original JiaMeng2022 arXiv2201.06748v1 p2','Original EsoleKang2018 arXiv1807.08755v1 pp3–4','PetersSterk June2024 author draft p61, Theorem2.2.1 and full proof'])
record('E.2.2','Checked every pointwise transversality case: if df is not onto, the value is one of the three exceptional points and dh is onto by hypothesis. Closedness in the compact product gives compactness. The two explicit inverse maps prove the literal product case. Integral Kunneth has no Tor contribution because H*(S6) is free; the fundamental group and Euler formulas follow. This is a complete elementary application, with no claim of new transversality or Kunneth theory.')
record('E.2.3','Read and rederived the entire group and rational Leray calculation. Each cusp kills its two angular generators and its meridian, and normal closure under A1 kills u; the finite gluing leaves central gamma,gamma-prime with the exact two3rd/fourth-power relations and product relation. The hyperbolic S2(3,4,3,4) orbifold has Euler-5/6; its principal torus orbibundle gives injection of the central Z². Recomputed the abelian relation matrix. The exterior direct-image Euler polynomial uses four finite and two cusp points; its H1 row and tensor transgression supports are correct. Even invariant-to-coinvariant pairings are nonzero and odd ones zero, so the displayed d2 ranks determine all Betti numbers without a degeneration assumption. Admissible Mobius transformations form a path-connected complex-hypersurface complement and proper smooth transport preserves orientation.', ['Original Scott hyperbolic-orbifold theorem opening','Exact rational matrix program rerun'], ['Original sphere transgressions are supplied by the complete PaperI topology proof'])
record('E.2.5','Read and checked the whole low-degree integral proof. The two-variable support-function line bundles supply the complete primitive cusp invariant lattice. Finite degree-one indices3/4 and degree-two order-two defect produce18 finite presentation rows; q1/q2 kill the two Z2 summands and gamma1*gamma2 removes one primitive order12 summand, leaving Z12^7. The parabolic H1 group is free once the global coboundary is primitive; its rank is18. The two original integral d2 maps hit the two primitive target summands separately, leaving E_infinity^(2,1)=0. The remaining H3 extension has free quotient and hence preserves exactly that torsion. UCT then gives the asserted H2.', ['fourfolds_shifted_integral.py exact Smith/primitivity rerun','Original X integral transgression in PaperI'], ['maps_B.tex lines966–1003: entire derivation of equationB.5.13 independently rederived; this is an equation tag, not a separate result'])
record('E.2.6','Read and checked every step of the full integral MV proof. The actual base-disc product decomposition retains full boundary markings and reverses only the normal circle. Sphere MV gives free Hk(E)=H(k-1)(T4) for1<=k<=4 and H>=5=0. Read/rederived equationB.5.13: mapping-torus Smith primitivity, invariant Gram determinants9/4, covering degrees3/4 and the(v2,d) torus condition a+b even. Complementary integral pairing then gives boundary image indices(12,2,2,12). Over a punctured disc each local generator is independent, so H2(D,j*L)=0 and local restrictions suffice. Boundary isotropy gives the rank-one adjoints c=(12eps,2eta,-2eta,-12eps). Rechecked both Koszul and orientation signs of every MV block; the two geometric signs are allowed independently in both pieces. A free MV kernel makes the final extension split, so the Smith torsion is actual homology and satisfies degree9-k torsion duality.', ['manifolds_shifted_mv.py full sixteen-sign Smith rerun and retained output'], ['maps_B.tex lines915–1040 opened for exact finite quotient lattice bases and the full B.5.13 calculation'])
record('E.2.7','Read and rederived the entire family-transport and tangent proof. The bad Mobius loci have real codimension two, and the vertical derivative of f1-f2 stays onto along an admissible path; compact lifted flow gives oriented diffeomorphism. The normal complex line is g*TB, whose integral c1 vanishes via H2(S6)=0, so it is trivial. Adding the two bounding sphere lines gives TP+R4=R14. The holomorphic exact tangent sequence independently yields integral c1=c2=0, without deducing complex Chern vanishings solely from stable real triviality.')
record('E.2.8','Read the complete disc-extension construction. B2.1 null-homotopy gives a smooth D7 extension fixed on a boundary collar. Relative transversality is required only at the second map’s three critical values. At all other values df2 is onto; at those three, dF is onto. The resulting eleven-dimensional inverse image has boundary exactly P and its inverse-image orientation agrees with the complex boundary orientation. The pulled-back normal2-plane comes from the contractible D7. Any two boundary choices agree up to homotopy because [S6,SO2]=H1(S6,Z)=0. The bounding second-sphere framing and outward collar normal give exactly the specified natural boundary stable framing.', ['Original Hirsch Chapter3 section2 Theorems2.1/2.5 and relative-cutoff hypotheses opening','B2.1 exact null-homotopy is assigned to maps_audit; retain its current gate'])
record('E.2.9','Read and rederived the full aspherical target and framed bordism proof. Weighted Hopf critical pairs are disjoint, so their fibre product is a smooth closed four-manifold. Primitive finite translations make the torus orbibundle total space smooth; the good hyperbolic orbifold cover is H² and its torus-bundle pullback is trivial, yielding universal cover H²×R². The literal quotient maps carry the exact six generators identically, so c induces the stated pi1 isomorphism. Abelian character(4,-3,-4,3,12,-12), duality and Euler0 give homology(S1×S3). The stable splitting(S3)+=S0∨S3 separates each bounding sphere’s zero component and the specific eta³ map component. All four external-product components vanish, the last by eta4=0. Transverse inverse image of N in a framed13-bordism has the required11-dimensional filling overBG, and the normal framing pulled from the first S3 agrees with E2.8 after pullback. This is a bordism statement only; no smooth classification is inferred.', ['Original Scott83 and Davis–Kirk01 theorem openings','Use the already opened IWX2023 Table1 p113 for pi4S=0, explicitly recording the different edition','B1.2 eta³ class and A2.1/B2.1 actual maps are assigned to maps_audit','shifted_group_bordism.py arithmetic rerun'])

record('E.2.10','Read and rederived the complete marked knot-group and both spinning obstructions. Removing the regular base disc leaves a^3=h,b^4=h^-1 and the unfilled meridian ab. The free-product quotient proves peripheral Z² injectivity. Its unique zero-linking framing has theta=-12gamma, so g maps to h*mu^-12 and u,w,d die. Boundary restrictions give -12gamma*u and -12gamma*w, forcing their common contraction radical into Z*d, while a degree-three class ±2gamma*u*w is killed by d. For an ordinary triple spin, the original longitude lies in the degree-two radical but remains nontrivial; for a single spin of arbitrary T3, the exact cap MV gives R²=R_L² and R³=R_L² wedge s, so contraction by the spin circle must be injective on R³. Both contradictions use the full embedded peripheral/zero-linking data, not merely the abstract knot group.', ['Winter2008 original ordinary-spin definition and Theorem4.5 opening','maps_shifted_pi2.py contraction certificate rerun'], ['E2.6 full marked boundary maps; B5.2 exact original cap presentation as separately assigned'])
record('E.2.11','Read and checked the entire homological, cohomological and module argument. The three retained degree-two boundary coordinates theta*g1,theta*g2,g1*g2 vanish on kerD2 in that order; naturality gives c_*H3=0. In target MV, the two primitive relations leave v=gamma1*gamma2 as the free H3 connecting generator; source images contain12v and every v coefficient is divisible by12, so c^* has exact order12. The relative universal-cover pair is2-connected and its degree-three Hurewicz group is pi2(P), so H3(N,P)=(pi2P)_G and H2(N,P)=0. UCT identifies evaluation on the injected z with12Z, forcing gcd(12,e1,...,e7)=1 in the complete extension presentation. Its Smith factors give Z²+Z12^6. A projective group-ring module would have free abelian coinvariants, and the specified connected sums add only free induced pi2 modules.', ['maps_shifted_pi2.py full integral boundary certificates rerun','E2.6 and E2.9 dependencies as separately scoped'])
record('E.2.12','Read all239 lines and rederived the actual group-ring localization proof. Explicit unimodular row/column operations reduce B(z) to diag(1,z-1,z-1) with one zero column; its transpose is injective. The infinite-cylinder normalization has no degree-two extension or possible higher differential, giving H2=A+(A/(z-1))² and H4=A. Injected central Z² makes R free over its Laurent subring, so localization is flat and both central differences are non-zero-divisors. Regular torus Koszul complexes contract after h1-1 inversion; finite caps have pure-translation mth powers and die. The sole surviving first cusp induces the two shifted T3 exterior algebras over R1/(h2-1), giving ranks1,3,4,4,3,1. Before localization the regular/boundary two-stage filtrations are killed by I², caps by q=(h1-1)(h2-1), and MV gives q²H*=0 without a splitting assumption. Infinite rank follows from the surviving central Laurent submodule, ruling out a finite-type universal cover and a compact-fibre pi1-isomorphic fibration overN.', ['manifolds_cusp_alexander.py exact Laurent matrix rerun','E2.9 central subgroup injection as separately scoped'])
record('E.2.13','Read and rederived the complete actual circle fibration and return argument. Averaging the integral primitive class over the torus action gives alpha(V1)=12 and alpha(V2)=-12. At every point an unchanged regular factor maps its g-vector to one of these fields, so the pulled-back form is nowhere zero on the actual map. Primitivity gives connected fibre. The mod12 cone-character kernel is torsion free with Euler-10 and genus6; its central kernel is generated by h1*h2. Independently checked the weighted Hopf connection and orientation integral1/12, yielding the two pulled-back Euler entries(-1,-1) and diagonal-circle Euler-1. Localizations force faithful action of the whole central Z² on pi2. Every finite-index subgroup has centralizer contained in this centre; an S1 product factor would contradict faithfulness. A stable letter of character1 acts inner on kerchi exactly when its exponent is divisible by12, while no positive return power is homotopic to identity.', ['Scott83 exact orbifold classification and Euler covering formula opening','maps_shifted_circle.py integral character/Euler rerun','A2.1 literal quotient-map derivative checked by maps_audit'])
record('E.2.14','Read all307 lines and checked the actual splice, return and rational variation. The two maps xi_E-12gamma2 and12gamma1-xi_E agree on the full product collar; their regular-circle derivatives stay nonzero. Their level is the connected E12 cover timesT3, with theta1prime=gamma2-gamma1 and opposite second marking. The interpolated vector field has d(rho)=1; its time12 map is exactly the primitive diagonal torus twist, identity at both collar ends. The deRham/prism variation is boundary-connecting composed with contraction and restriction, so its square vanishes. Noninvariant deck eigenspaces restrict to zero, making the displayed invariant boundary matrices sufficient for the variation. Recomputed the ring-product sign normalization c2=-2,c3=2. The actual affine character transports are lambda^4 A1^-t,lambda^-3 A2^-t,M0^-t, and the punctured-disc graph has no H2. Summing the six character-order rows with multiplicities1,1,2,2,2,4 gives E12 ranks(1,7,46,56,46,6,0). MV then gives the stated fibre Betti vector; Wang fixes precisely one size-two eigenvalue-one Jordan block in degrees4/5, all other blocks semisimple.', ['maps_shifted_return.py and maps_shifted_cover.py full exact matrix reruns','Original sphere integral cusp specialization is in the separately checked B5.16 context'])
record('E.2.15','Read the entire integral proof and checked all extension arguments. The regular permutation coefficient lattice avoids integral averaging: finite lifted caps are genuine torus root covers and cusp sheets unchanged, so each stalk is the primitive invariant lattice. Hermite bases of im(T_i-I) preserve indices in the graph map; its Smith primitivity must be checked by the retained program. Free E12 groups imply free piece relative groups by Poincare–Lefschetz, so the actual boundary image is the saturation of its known rational span. The common-boundary lattice is obtained from ker[A,-B] because each A/B is an injective column basis. Integral prism variation applies also to possible torsion output; rank-one Smith72 in degrees4/5 lies in a primitive free MV summand. A primitive factorization72*u*ell with ell(u)=0 yields the stated shear normal form. Wang gives all covers; only degrees3/7 have a potentially absorbing torsion extension, and the10-dimensional integral linking pairing fixes them from the already settled degrees8/4. UCT gives exactly the homological torsion list and the distinguishing order72n.', ['maps_shifted_cover_integral.py and maps_shifted_fibre_integral.py complete Hermite/Smith transforms rerun','E2.14 actual collar and E12 boundary marking'])

record('E.2.16','Read all429 lines and rederived the derived cusp comparison and full integral presentation. The boundary mapping cone has H1=A/(q²)+A/(q); the actual normalized component intersections give 2-h-h^-1, hence a unit Ext1 component modulo q². Since all displayed homology modules have projective dimension at most one, the derived splitting and triangular target changes remove exactly the stated extension components while preserving the full external map. Every unit modulo q² lifts to ±h^n. The terminal-strip exterior chain lift and the finite winding norm use the actual maps, with the negative fourth-root norm and phase-degree norms kept distinct. Checked injectivity of the Fox column via (a-1)N_a=q, the pure augmentation reductions, and both redundant final relations. The induced cyclic-sign extension has nonzero class in Z/2, preserves the injection of the invariant infinite-order t, and gives the equivalent cyclic presentation after replacing x by x+t. The peripheral homology and all ten degree-two chain columns are retained separately; the nonzero free coefficient on gTheta is not discarded.', ['maps_complement_module.py exact noncommutative chain/cancellation/peripheral certificate source reading and rerun','E2.12 exact Laurent calculation and original cusp specialization equationsB.5.16–17'], ['Full source maps_complement_module.tex, including the actual terminal-strip comparison and final peripheral prism identity'])
record('E.2.17','Read all380 lines and rederived the kernel-complex construction and every abstract module reduction. The complement projection to its one-relator aspherical spine keeps the actual Fox peripheral column; its degree-two Fox column is injective, so projection extends over the full higher complex. The aspherical splice target retains its degree-four cell, avoiding a false truncated acyclicity argument. The degreewise split kernel has six unit degree-one pairs; after cancellation its H2 is the explicit34-by123 presentation. Both normal-circle inversion and product-order signs were checked. Pure norm relations kill the previously unassigned central differences before passing to the orbifold group ring. The seven-generator change has determinant1; substituting its inverse gives t1=OmegaL and eliminates that generator with a unit coefficient. The two cyclic axes have no common central kernel. Coinvariants give six Z12 factors. Restricting to the actual circle-fibre group has index12 on each axis because chi(hi)=±12 and injects there; hence24 free group-ring generators. The remaining surface-group restriction and its144-by240 exact Smith calculation are separate from any smooth-type assertion.', ['maps_splice_module.py exact amalgam normal form, full presentation reductions and coinvariant Smith certificate source reading/rerun','E2.16 full peripheral comparison'])
record('E.2.18','Read all305 source lines, including the concluding scope restriction, and rederived the natural quadratic image and both universal connected-sum obstructions. The normalized curve relations give free AE1 plus two A/(h-1) classes; surjectivity and the ordinary phase comparison fix the free unit and both torsion coordinates, so translating the component yields the complete normalization map. Substitution into q(H)-sum q(Ei) gives -[E,U]-2q(D); the tracked actual cusp cycles then give [e(h-1),t]-12q(t). The infinite-order invariant t makes this mixed term nonzero. The index12 subgroup F6×Z proves residual finiteness of K and direct finiteness of ZK, so every rank-one free splitting has exactly the asserted complementary torsion module. For Y the actual inclusion maps identify both invariant ti; their coinvariant images have order6. Any free retraction would force every coefficient vj(z-1) divisible by6, and injectivity of z-1 in (Z/6)[Pi] then contradicts sum vj*uj=1. The lifted connected-sum four-skeleton has zero mixed Whitehead component, including for arbitrary choices of free summand. This proves only the stated obstruction and specified quadratic image.', ['Original Whitehead1950 Theorems1/5 and section2 opening','maps_cusp_quadratic.py and maps_splice_quadratic.py exact tracked-cycle certificates source reading/rerun','D1.9 full wall-degree orientation comparison is assigned to invariants_arithmetic'])
record('E.2.19','Read all212 lines and checked the actual smooth-family and framing argument. Scaling the bounded analytic period correction gives a smooth family of free toric deck actions. Orthogonality of B0 and T>K+1 give uniform lattice nondegeneracy; the bounded finite chart estimate supplies a compact quotient through q=0. A horizontal vector field extends the prescribed real boundary marking, stays tangent to every toric stratum, and gives a relative orientation-preserving smooth comparison. The six fan cones are unimodular; the principal central divisor gives normal bundle KS, with each surface-normal and canonical restriction of degree-1. The map(z,a,b)↦(1/z,zb,za) preserves q, is involutive and has complex determinant1. Actual translated fan matrices give the cyclic triple-coordinate return, not merely an unframed graph identification. The clockwise q-loop is matched to the exact M0 endpoint convention. No logarithmic homeomorphism is promoted to a smooth map.', ['maps_cusp_smooth_plumbing.py exact six-chart, normal-degree, triple-cycle and boundary-marking certificate source reading/rerun'])
record('E.2.20','Read all200 lines including the post-proof high-handle qualification. The invariant normal coordinate r=s*exp(2pi*i*kappa*gamma(x)) cancels the finite quotient phase because kappa²=1, and the inverse is independent of representatives. In the adapted lattice sigma=m*kappa*phi produces exactly the stated mapping torus. Substitution of the actual boundary drift cancels theta in the normal angle; both angular matrices are unimodular and the seam uses Bj^-1. The function q=r^m exp(-2pi*i*sigma) gives the actual positive meridian vj-m*rhoj. The core zero section, collar drift removal and E2.19 relative cusp comparison glue with all boundary markings fixed. The hemisphere decomposition then reverses only the normal angle. The final index bound is justified: absolute indices at most4 would give only relative indices at least2 and force boundary pi1 surjectivity, contradicting the actual knot-group marking.', ['maps_finite_cap_framings.py full affine/seam/meridian certificate source reading/rerun','B5.1 full collar drift isotopy is assigned to maps_audit','E2.19 relative smooth cusp comparison'])
record('E.2.21','Read all487 lines and rederived the entire geometric prescription and relative smooth comparison. The product-radius domains are rounded balls by positive radial derivatives, with rescaling linear near the origin and fixed on attaching collars. The annular endpoints retain both unit angular rotations and all six actual placements. The log-sum-exponential moment Hessian is positive definite and gives a diffeomorphism to the hexagon interior; q itself trivializes the canonical line on the free torus locus. Compatible nested stratum cuts leave exactly the dense T²-times-disc block, and properness excludes any omitted component or handle after shrinking the common q-disc. Every sector is the actual unimodular monomial chart, with telescoping seams and prescribed normal multiplier. Iterated two-semicircle decomposition gives ordinary handles with explicit new endpoint faces, not just handle counts. The incoming cusp/core has two surface strips; the finite cap relative blocks include the normal disc and its full inverse angular map. Recomputed counts(2,5,14,22,21,10,2), product/dual polynomial and orientation sign(-1)^24. The final relative uniqueness argument extends the explicit full attaching isotopies by a cutoff and retains all top-handle and belt embeddings; no arbitrary sphere capping is introduced.', ['Original Vogel2009 section4.1 equation16 and Milnor1965 Theorems1.4/3.13/5.8 opening','maps_ordinary_handles.py full endpoint/sector/handle-list certificate source reading/rerun','E2.19–20 actual relative smooth comparisons'])
record('E.2.4','Read the complete synthesis statement together with every line of its actual proof E2.21 and prerequisites E2.19–20. Its76-handle relative complement and2432-handle shifted product are exactly the objects defined by the full framed coordinate prescription; it introduces no additional independent theorem requiring a missing proof. The referenced complex/topological and quadratic conclusions remain distinct results and their individual audit scopes are retained.', ['E2.21 original-source and exact-program checks as individually recorded'], ['fourfolds.tex lines625–647 and complete maps_ordinary_handles.tex'])

